  "findings": [
    "The generated linear winding network agrees with independent common-mode, differential-mode and reversed-dot analytical impedances.",
    "All selected hypotheses pass the existing fixture checks; these check sampled levels, release crossings, timestep refinement and doubled cable load, not absolute transient voltage limits.",
    "Negative cable-voltage extrema vary materially despite similar release intervals. Coupling cannot be dismissed from release intervals alone.",
    "Dot choices and coupling are hypotheses. Receiver protection, nonlinear ferrite behavior, parasitics and physical winding parameters remain unqualified. Firmware runners still use the uncoupled default."
  ],
